# derived rate data (regenerable; contains client billing patterns)
# `data/*` and not `data/`, because git cannot re-include anything under an excluded
# DIRECTORY — the negation below is silently dead against `data/`. The corpus and test set
# are large and regenerable; a Leg C result is neither. The 2026-09-03 run's number was
# bought with real model calls, written to .tmp-data, wiped, and six weeks later nobody
# could find it, so the study was nearly re-run from scratch for an answer already paid for.
data/*
!data/study/

# import-ready workflow with secret baked in (never commit)
n8n/*.local.json

# live-workflow snapshots: the POST-to-Engine / Dedupe-Claim nodes carry
# N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET in their headers, so these must never be committed.
# (The one pre-existing snapshot below predates that node and is clean.)
n8n/backups/*.json
!n8n/backups/bookings-CPIRu7CpezvKjU8d.backup.json

# session scratch: debug probes plus cached client corpora (emails, places,
# rate pairs). Same reason data/ is ignored — regenerable, and it is client data.
.tmp-data/
